Article 8 (Duties of Registration Authorities)
(1) An institution designated as a registration authority shall perform the duties under paragraph (2) after obtaining a certificate from the Certification Management Center.
(2) A registration authority shall perform the following duties:
1. Registration and deletion of subscribing agencies, etc., and changes to related registration information;
2. Verification of the identities of subscribing agencies, etc.;
3. Receipt and review of applications for issuance of certificates, and forwarding of the applications to the Certification Management Center;
4. Receipt and review of applications for revocation of certificates, and forwarding of the applications to the Certification Management Center;
5. Deleted. <November 6, 2019>
(3) A registration authority shall securely manage the administrative digital-signature generation key associated with a certificate issued by the certification authority so that the key is not lost, damaged, stolen, or disclosed. <Newly Inserted on November 6, 2019>
